    problem="The operator must split a path into its directory and its filename. Candidates: string-index-right on the separator (finds the boundary that actually separates them), string-index (finds the FIRST slash, which splits after the top-level directory and is wrong for every nested path), or string-split then reassemble (correct, allocates a list and then rebuilds most of it). For a last-occurrence boundary, string-index-right is the honest verb.",
